# Analysis

You're absolutely right. The `ResizeObserver` is **redundant and causing the bug**. 

The sidebar has an explicit `toggleCollapse()` button that lets users manually control the collapsed state. The ResizeObserver then **auto-collapses on resize**, which:

1. Overwrites the user's manual preference during mount
2. Causes the restored state to be ignored
3. Creates conflicting state management (user intent vs. auto-collapse logic)

**Solution:** Remove ResizeObserver entirely. Keep only manual toggle control via the button.

---

## Changes

| File | Change | Reason |
|------|--------|--------|
| `src/store/ui.js` | Remove `sidebarInitialized` flag (no longer needed) | Simplify state after removing auto-collapse logic |
| `src/store/ui.js` | Simplify `setSidebarCollapsed()` to always save | No guard condition needed |
| `src/components/layout/DesktopSidebar.vue` | Remove `setupResizeObserver()` method | Delete auto-collapse logic |
| `src/components/layout/DesktopSidebar.vue` | Remove `resizeObserver` data and lifecycle hooks | Clean up unused code |

---

## Implementation

```js src/store/ui.js
